WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:14.899
Welcome to SuiFleet. Start here to connect the account that
manages your devices. Your wallet is the approval tool for
changes such as registering devices and deploying software.
Choose Connect Wallet, then pick your sign-in method.

2
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:26.416
This demonstration uses a scripted test wallet. In your own
session, your wallet asks you to approve the connection. Read
each request so you know which account you are connecting.

3
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:39.259
After connecting, check the account and network shown here. This
guide uses testnet, where the tokens are for testing. Confirming
these details helps you avoid making changes with the wrong
account.

4
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:52.120
A fleet is a workspace for a set of devices and their management
settings. On your first visit, create the default fleet and
approve the request. This gives you a workspace to organize your
devices.

5
00:00:52.840 --> 00:01:05.811
The fleet switcher shows which workspace you are managing. Check
it before making changes, especially if your account manages
several fleets. With your account connected and fleet selected,
you can fund the network budget.

